<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30065" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murrātus</span></b>  (less correctly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myrrhā-tus</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Spiced</i> or <i>mingled with
			myrrh</i> (post-class.): potio, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				158</span></i> Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Marc. 15, 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Anointed with balsam of myrrh</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Satiapae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
